steps.text:
W′ isn't spent only once. Below CP it refills, quickly at first and then more slowly; the further below CP you recover, the faster it comes back [[c:wbal-recharge]]. Tracked second by second, it is [W′ balance](g:w-prime-balance) (W′bal; see the critical power module). In field trials of athletes doing irregular efforts, the model predicted when W′ was nearly empty and exhaustion close [[c:wbal-predict]].

For pacing this turns a feeling into a plan:

- every surge, attack or climb above CP draws on the same budget;
- after going deep to close a gap, you need time well below CP before the next effort;
- on a hilly course the climbs are the best place to spend it (next card).
